Hair: auburn hair, shaved at the sides with a longer top;
Eyes: golden-brown;
Skin: warm copper-brown;
Scars: Two small pale lines over the left knuckles from a pre-camp accident.;

Origin: Born human with an awakened internal magical spark and a spirit capable of consciously channeling Wild/Natural magical energy.;
Place of Birth: Detroit, Michigan;
Birthdate: February 8, 2007;

Personality: Sofia is recklessly funny. They are charismatic, creative, and socially fearless. Around trusted cabinmates they loosen noticeably, but conflict exposes the harder edge of their personality: they uses humor to dodge accountability. They are capable of humor, tenderness, jealousy, boredom, anger, attraction, and poor judgment rather than functioning as a single supernatural stereotype.;

Strengths: Charismatic, creative, and socially fearless. Sofia is especially reliable when a situation requires patience, reading a room, or committing to a decision once they have made it.;
Weaknesses: Bloodburn, overcasting, distraction, broken concentration, anti-magic, and ordinary human physical vulnerability. Personally, Sofia is most destabilized by being sent home as a failure.;
Flaws: Uses humor to dodge accountability. They can rationalize this flaw as self-protection long after it starts hurting other people.;
Fears: Being sent home as a failure. The fear affects their choices without controlling every scene.;
Quirks: Names pieces of training equipment.;
Habits: Falls asleep with music still playing.;
Powers: Innate spellcasting through an internal magical reservoir; trained in wards, elemental shaping, ritual construction, counter-magic, and short-range shadow stepping.;
Unique Triats: Has a recognizable magical signature and an unusually strong intuitive affinity for short-range shadow stepping. Their current individual specialty is short-range shadow stepping, giving their power use a personal style instead of making them interchangeable with others of the same race.;

Education: Camp Mystic Five-Year Residential Program — Year 2; G-01 Moonflower Cabin. Finished high school through a hybrid online program and is exploring vocational certificates.;
Training: Current Camp Mystic training includes reservoir control, spell precision, ritual safety, counter-magic, and short-range shadow stepping, emergency shutdown procedure, consent law, feeding/donor safety where relevant, and independent-living preparation.;
Past Occupation/Role: Currently a Camp Mystic camper; previously student and part-time retail employee.;

Physical Skills: Sofia has solid camp-level conditioning, swimming and first-aid basics, plus above-average coordination from repeated control drills. Their strongest non-supernatural physical skill is distance running.;

Personal Items of Note: A pair of expensive noise-canceling headphones.;
Favorite Things: Crafts, fruit candy, and ridiculous reality television.;
Pet Peeves: Someone changing agreed plans at the last second.;

Fun Fact: Knows every shortcut between the Rec Hall and the lake.;
Secret: Sofia keeps a second phone their family does not know about.;
Philosophy: "Home is the place where you are known accurately.";
Motivation: Prove they can control their power without becoming emotionally numb.;

Backstory: Sofia grew up in a highly controlled supernatural family and came to camp partly to learn who they are without family expectations. A magical incident proved that theory and raw talent were not enough without structured control and legal understanding. They entered Moonflower Cabin expecting Camp Mystic to feel like exile. By Year 2, the camp has become a complicated mix of refuge, frustration, friendship, and unfinished work. Their story is not about becoming harmless; it is about becoming responsible without losing the parts of themselves that make life worth having.;

